Then open README.md and confirm each matched heading starts a section with text describing that function.
PASS: prints `missing README sections: none`, `exit=0`, and every exported function (it should include at least capitalize, slugify, truncate, padLeft) has a heading with a description under it. FAIL: any function listed as missing (note: slugify had no section before this change, so it must be added too), nonzero exit, or a heading with no describing text.

Check 4 — expect: "npm test passes"
Run: `npm test; echo exit=$?`
PASS: `exit=0` and the output shows `# fail 0`. FAIL: nonzero exit or any failing test.

